plvm: an optional op profile, by module bytecode offset

A plvm built with -DPLVM_PROFILE counts the ops it runs at each offset
of each loaded module's bytecode, and at exit, if the environment
variable PLVM_PROFILE names a file, writes the counts there. A normal
build is unchanged. With a listing of a module's bytecode, the counts
show where a program spends its time: ccish's tools/profile.py
(make profile) maps them to functions.

To build one, from src/, after the patch:

    cc -DPLVM_PROFILE vmsrc/plvm.c vmsrc/cmdsys.c vmsrc/sysio.c \
       vmsrc/a1cffa.c vmsrc/lib6502/lib6502.a -o plvmprof

The file it writes: for each module, "module NAME LENGTH", then
"OFFSET COUNT" for each offset that ran (offsets from the module's
first bytecode byte); last, "other COUNT", the ops run outside any
module's bytecode.

This is ccish's copy, which ccish's tools/profile.py applies to a copy
of src/vmsrc (with patch -p3); src/vmsrc itself isn't changed. Apply
it to a PLASMA tree with patch -p1 from the top.

